# env.mask -- CEO-409 line masks, declared beside the data (FORMAT: entry<TAB>L<n>-or-python-regex<TAB>reason).
# env.icn prints the running machine, clock and environment by design; everything else it prints -- the layout and the
# ten &features words -- is graded. Measured 2026-09-28 (hq_icon): iconx run twice, minutes apart and with HOME=/tmp
# SHELL=/bin/sh on the second run, moved lines 3 5 18 19; line 4 moves by the day; lines 2 and 20 are the host and kernel.
env	L2	ampersand-host is the running machine's name (env.icn reports its environment by design)
env	L3	ampersand-dateline moves with the clock (measured: 8:51 am vs 8:54 am on two iconx runs)
env	L4	ampersand-date moves with the calendar day
env	L5	ampersand-clock moves with the clock (measured: 08:51:47 vs 08:54:14 on two iconx runs)
env	L6	ampersand-version is implementation-defined (CEO-409): iconx names Icon 9.5.25a, SCRIP its own version string
env	L18	getenv HOME is the running user's (measured: /home/satirical vs /tmp under HOME=/tmp)
env	L19	getenv SHELL is the running user's (measured: /bin/bash vs /bin/sh under SHELL=/bin/sh)
env	L20	uname -a is the running kernel and host
